IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Defence Forces Special Retirement Benefits Act 1960 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE
-- RULES AND THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source:
-- ../registers/source-bundle/C1960A00068.txt (compilation prepared on 19
-- April 2001). Commenced (the proclaimed date) on 1 February 1961. The soldier
-- discharged in the 1961 reduction asks: "Does the Act apply to me; what
-- gratuity or pension do I get?" Amounts are in pounds, as printed.

§ `Nouns`

-- s 3(2)(b), First Schedule.
DECLARE `Category` IS ONE OF
    `category 101`, `category 102`, `category 103`, `category 104`, `category 105`,
    `category 106`, `category 107`, `category 108`, `category 109`

-- s 10(2).
DECLARE `Section 10 contributor` IS ONE OF
    `not contributing on retirement for additional benefits`
    `contributing on retirement for additional benefits`

DECLARE `Soldier case` HAS
    -- s 4(2)
    `on 1 February 1961 I was a male Regular Army member contributing to the Fund` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was in the Royal Australian Army Ordnance Corps`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `my engagement expires on`                                      IS A DATE
    `I was an officer during the prescribed period`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `my date of birth`                                              IS A DATE
    `the Minister declared me to be discharged for reduction`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was discharged on`                                           IS A DATE
    `I was discharged for the reduction`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `I became a member again the next day`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    -- ss 5-10
    `completed years of service for pension`                        IS A NUMBER
    `I would have completed 20 years' service by age 55`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `my category`                                                   IS A `Category`
    -- s 7(2): daily rate of active pay, in pounds
    `my daily rate of active pay`                                   IS A NUMBER
    -- ss 9-10: the Board's figures, in pounds a year or pounds
    `I am a reduced benefit contributor`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Board's maximum pension rate`                              IS A NUMBER
    `the minimum pension rate`                                      IS A NUMBER
    `the maximum additional pension contribution`                   IS A NUMBER
    `section 10 contributor`                                        IS A `Section 10 contributor`
    `the normal pension rate`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `the normal additional pension contribution`                    IS A NUMBER
    -- ss 9(5), 10(5)
    `the Board's statement was served on`                           IS A DATE
    `I paid a contribution on`                                      IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the contribution I paid`                                       IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Benefit` IS ONE OF
    `none under this Act`
    `a gratuity under section 6`
    `a gratuity under section 7`
    `a pension under section 9`
    `a pension under section 10`

DECLARE `Soldier position` HAS
    `the Act applies to me`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `my benefit`                                                    IS A `Benefit`
    `the special gratuity in pounds`                                IS A NUMBER
    `my pension rate in pounds a year`                              IS A NUMBER
    `the prescribed day for my contribution`                        IS A MAYBE DATE

§ `Rules`

`the proclaimed date` MEANS Date 1 2 1961

-- s 4(1): nine months for the Ordnance Corps, otherwise three, commencing on
-- the proclaimed date: to 31 October 1961 or 30 April 1961.
@ref s 4(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Soldier case`
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the prescribed period for` c MEANS
    IF c's `I was in the Royal Australian Army Ordnance Corps`
    THEN Date 31 10 1961
    ELSE Date 30 4 1961

GIVEN c IS A `Soldier case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `discharged within the period` c IF
        c's `I was discharged on` AT LEAST `the proclaimed date`
    AND c's `I was discharged on` AT MOST `the end of the prescribed period for` c

-- s 4(2)(a)-(f).
@ref s 4(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Soldier case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to` c IF
        c's `on 1 February 1961 I was a male Regular Army member contributing to the Fund`
    AND c's `my engagement expires on` GREATER THAN `the end of the prescribed period for` c
    AND NOT (c's `I was an officer during the prescribed period`)
    AND `add months` (c's `my date of birth`) 660 GREATER THAN `the end of the prescribed period for` c
    AND c's `the Minister declared me to be discharged for reduction`
    AND `discharged within the period` c
    AND c's `I was discharged for the reduction`
    AND NOT (c's `I became a member again the next day`)

-- ss 6, 7, 9, 10: the benefit follows the completed years of service.
@ref ss 6, 7, 9(1), 10(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Soldier case`
GIVETH A `Benefit`
`my benefit for` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the Act applies to` c) THEN `none under this Act`
        IF c's `completed years of service for pension` LESS THAN 6 THEN `a gratuity under section 6`
        IF c's `completed years of service for pension` AT LEAST 20 THEN `a pension under section 10`
        IF c's `completed years of service for pension` AT LEAST 15 AND c's `I would have completed 20 years' service by age 55`
            THEN `a pension under section 9`
        OTHERWISE `a gratuity under section 7`

-- s 6: £20 for each completed year. s 7(1)(b), (2): the years times 14 times
-- (the daily rate of active pay plus 10s 6d, that is £0.525).
@ref ss 6, 7
GIVEN c IS A `Soldier case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the special gratuity for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER `my benefit for` c
    WHEN `a gratuity under section 6` THEN 20 TIMES c's `completed years of service for pension`
    WHEN `a gratuity under section 7` THEN
        c's `completed years of service for pension` TIMES 14 TIMES (c's `my daily rate of active pay` PLUS 0.525)
    OTHERWISE 0

-- First Schedule: the maximum pension rate for 15 to 19 completed years.
@ref First Schedule
GIVEN k IS A `Category`, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the First Schedule rate for` k `after` y MEANS
    `base for` k PLUS (y MINUS 15) TIMES `step for` k

GIVEN k IS A `Category`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`base for` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `category 101` THEN 400
    WHEN `category 102` THEN 365
    WHEN `category 103` THEN 345
    WHEN `category 104` THEN 330
    WHEN `category 105` THEN 310
    WHEN `category 106` THEN 295
    WHEN `category 107` THEN 275
    WHEN `category 108` THEN 260
    WHEN `category 109` THEN 245

GIVEN k IS A `Category`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`step for` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `category 101` THEN 20
    WHEN `category 102` THEN 18
    WHEN `category 103` THEN 17
    WHEN `category 104` THEN 16
    WHEN `category 105` THEN 15
    WHEN `category 106` THEN 14
    WHEN `category 107` THEN 13
    WHEN `category 108` THEN 12
    WHEN `category 109` THEN 11

-- ss 9(2), 10(2): "the day occurring one month after service" of the Board's
-- statement.
@ref ss 9(2), 10(2) prescribed day
GIVEN c IS A `Soldier case`
GIVETH A DATE
`the prescribed day for` c MEANS `add months` (c's `the Board's statement was served on`) 1

-- ss 9(5), 10(5): only a contribution paid before the prescribed day counts.
GIVEN c IS A `Soldier case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the contribution in time for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `I paid a contribution on`
    WHEN JUST d THEN IF d LESS THAN `the prescribed day for` c THEN c's `the contribution I paid` ELSE 0
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0

-- min + (max - min) × paid / full, at most max.
GIVEN lo IS A NUMBER, hi IS A NUMBER, pd IS A NUMBER, full IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`scale from` lo `to` hi `paying` pd `of` full MEANS
    IF pd AT LEAST full OR full AT MOST 0 THEN hi
    ELSE lo PLUS (hi MINUS lo) TIMES pd DIVIDED BY full

-- s 9(2) maximum pension rate: the First Schedule, or the Board's figure for a
-- reduced benefit contributor. s 9(5)(a)-(c).
@ref s 9(2), (5)
GIVEN c IS A `Soldier case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 9 rate for` c MEANS
    `scale from` (c's `the minimum pension rate`) `to` hi `paying` (`the contribution in time for` c) `of` (c's `the maximum additional pension contribution`)
    WHERE
        hi MEANS
            IF c's `I am a reduced benefit contributor`
            THEN c's `the Board's maximum pension rate`
            ELSE `the First Schedule rate for` (c's `my category`) `after` (c's `completed years of service for pension`)

-- s 10(5)(a)-(f).
@ref s 10(5)
GIVEN c IS A `Soldier case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 10 rate for` c MEANS
    IF c's `section 10 contributor` EQUALS `not contributing on retirement for additional benefits`
    THEN `scale from` (c's `the minimum pension rate`) `to` (c's `the Board's maximum pension rate`) `paying` (`the contribution in time for` c) `of` (c's `the maximum additional pension contribution`)
    ELSE `the contributing rate for` c

-- s 10(5)(a), (c)-(f) for a person contributing for additional benefits.
@ref s 10(5)(a), (c)-(f)
GIVEN c IS A `Soldier case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the contributing rate for` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF pd AT LEAST full THEN hi
        IF pd AT LEAST normalc
            THEN `scale from` normalr `to` hi `paying` (pd MINUS normalc) `of` (full MINUS normalc)
        OTHERWISE `scale from` lo `to` normalr `paying` pd `of` normalc
    WHERE
        lo MEANS c's `the minimum pension rate`
        hi MEANS c's `the Board's maximum pension rate`
        pd MEANS `the contribution in time for` c
        full MEANS c's `the maximum additional pension contribution`
        normalr MEANS c's `the normal pension rate`
        normalc MEANS c's `the normal additional pension contribution`

GIVEN c IS A `Soldier case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my pension rate for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER `my benefit for` c
    WHEN `a pension under section 9` THEN `the section 9 rate for` c
    WHEN `a pension under section 10` THEN `the section 10 rate for` c
    OTHERWISE 0

@ref ss 4-10, First Schedule
@export default The benefit of a Regular Army soldier discharged in the 1961 reduction under the Defence Forces Special Retirement Benefits Act 1960 (Cth): whether the Act applies (s 4: a male contributing member on 1 February 1961, declared and discharged for the reduction within 3 months, or 9 for the Ordnance Corps, not an officer, under 55, engagement not expiring and not re-enlisting); then by completed years of service for pension: under 6, a gratuity of £20 a year (s 6); 6 to 14 (or 15 to 19 without reaching 20 by 55), a gratuity of 14 times the daily active pay plus 10s 6d for each year (s 7); 15 to 19, a pension at the First Schedule rate scaled by the contribution paid before the prescribed day (s 9); 20 or more, a pension under s 10 scaled the same way; and the prescribed day, one month after the Board's statement. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Soldier case`  @desc My service on 1 February 1961, discharge, years of service, category, pay, the Board's figures and statement, and my contribution
GIVETH A `Soldier position`
`the soldier position for` c MEANS
    `Soldier position` OF `the Act applies to` c, `my benefit for` c, `the special gratuity for` c, `my pension rate for` c,
                          (IF `my benefit for` c EQUALS `a pension under section 9` OR `my benefit for` c EQUALS `a pension under section 10`
                           THEN JUST (`the prescribed day for` c) ELSE NOTHING)
